# Settlement approval chain (16 Nov 2026). Same as UAT (done there through the
# connector). A settlement request -- the AI-checked bills on a rep's open
# settlement claim, or a cash advance -- goes up the requester's reporting line
# (BE > ABM > RBM > SM/ZSM > GM > CEO); the CEO's approval is final: the bills
# are Verified, or the advance goes to Accounts to pay. A reject (with a
# reason) sends it back to the requester.
#
#   1. DocTypes "Settlement Step", "Settlement Bill" (child tables) and
#      "Settlement Request" (SR-#####; System Manager only, HR / Accounts
#      Manager read) -- written only by the API below.
#   2. Expense Claim Detail: custom_settlement (Link) and the bill statuses
#      Checked and In Approval; Employee Advance.custom_task when missing.
#   3. Server Script "Settlement API" (API, method settlement) -- source
#      share/src/app/expense-claims/server/settlement_api.py.
#   4. "Expense Running Guard": the AI result makes a bill Checked (it no
#      longer verifies it); Checked bills may still change; the API's states
#      are locked. "Employee Advance Task": no Task for a cash request still
#      in the chain. Sources: expense_running_console.py (GUARD, ADVANCE_TASK).
#
# Paste into ERP > System Console (type Python), logged in as a System Manager.
# 1) DRY = True, "Commit" unticked: only prints.  2) DRY = False, tick Commit.
# Safe to re-run. After running: Frappe Cloud -> Clear Cache.

